  "_comment": "Hand-built 5x7 example (canonical GameState JSON). Imperius player; Odum (2,2 capital) and Nobu (2,5). City leveling: starts at level 1; level L→L+1 needs L+1 population (1→2 needs 2, 2→3 needs 3, …). A level-x city has x+1 bar slots (unit capacity). Cumulative pop to just reach level x is the x-th triangle number minus 1 (T(x)-1 = 2+3+…+x). Excess that does not trigger another level-up is stored in population (blue fill); a deficit vs that baseline is a red (negative) fill. Cities always level up when they have enough pop, so population is only the leftover. This scene: Nobu cumulative 6 = 2+3+1 → level 3, population 1 (4 bars); Odum cumulative 11 = 2+3+4+2 → level 4, population 2 (5 bars). Field names match pyrender_UPDATED/gamestate.py (IL2CPP snake_case).",
